Package: replayr
Title: Read Input Recordings of Video Games
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R:
    person("Thorben", "Pelzer", , "thorben@pelzer.blog",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5039-3779"))
Description: Imports input recordings and demo files of video games, as made
    in tool-assisted speedrunning, reinforcement learning, and research on
    human-game interaction. Reads the formats of 'FCEUX', 'BizHawk',
    'Dolphin', 'Citra', 'libTAS', 'openMSX', 'JPC-RR', 'Gym Retro', the
    'Doom' and 'GoldSrc' engines, and other recording tools. Platforms
    include the Atari 2600, Nintendo, Sega, and Sony consoles, arcade
    machines, and personal computers. Imported recordings keep compact
    digital control arrays, stable control identities, original numeric
    channels, metadata, and emulator commands. Supports gamepads,
    keyboards, mice, touchscreens, and recorded motion or light-gun
    channels. Source timing distinguishes frames, controller polls, and
    timestamped events. Left and right stick directions, angles, and
    magnitudes can be selected independently. Allows analysis of input
    recordings without running an emulator.
